 "notModeled": [
  "analog: PGA, input multiplexer and test connections, modulator, offset option (stored only); the result is the 0 V code",
  "digital filter: sinc / FIR / IIR high-pass stages, linear or minimum phase, HPF corner (HPF0/HPF1) and the 63-reading filter settling after SYNC, reset, wake-up or a register write (conversion time = 1 / data rate per Tables of sinc and FIR data rates at fCLK = 1.024 MHz)",
  "read-data-continuous vs read-data-by-command: the conversion data are always shifted out from CS fall (RDATAC behaviour, the power-on default); in SDATAC mode the part outputs nothing until RDATA, and SDATAC is cancelled by CS high; RDATA's data appear only when DRDY next falls (0..1 data period), the model replies at once",
  "DRDY: returns high on the first SCLK falling edge of any transfer (modeled as clears on read); with no read it pulses high for 4 fCLK before the next update (modeled as clears on start)",
  "STANDBY is cancelled when CS goes high (the model needs WAKEUP); PWDN low also resets the registers (modeled as power-down only)",
  "SYNC pin: pulse-sync vs continuous-sync mode (CONFIG0.SYNC); every SYNC rising edge restarts the conversion in the model",
  "offset and gain calibration (OFSCAL/GANCAL and the OFC/FSC scaling of the result)",
  "ID bits ID[3:0] are factory-programmed and undocumented (reset value x0h): modeled as 0",
  "24 fCLK minimum delay between command bytes, serial-port auto timeout (SCLK low for 64 DRDY periods), SCLK rate limits",
  "the internal 'registers written -> conversion restart' is modeled with write:REG start triggers",
  "the 32-bit result's LSB is a redundant sign bit (0 for the 0 V code)",
  "high-resolution vs low-power mode (ID_CFG.MODE21 / CONFIG0.MODE0): power and decimation only, the data rates are the same",
  "CONFIG1.BIAS must be written 1 after power-on/reset (stored only); 50 mV offset option"
 ],
